            <ArticleTitle>The buttonhole technique for arteriovenous fistula cannulation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>299-304</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The buttonhole technique began 30 years ago in Europe and Japan, and 25 years ago in Seattle, Washington. Some believe its failure to &quot;catch on&quot; in the United States is due to the graft culture of the last 20 years. Now with an increase of AV fustulae, this technique is becoming known as a viable cannulation option. The purpose of this article is to provide technical information for nephrology nurses performing this technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
